content.text:
Good question. Here's how both would look concretely:

## Option 2: Global `~/.claude/settings.json`

This would mean merging the Entire hooks into your existing global hooks. The key challenge is that `entire` must run from inside the git repo, so every hook command needs a `cd` prefix:

```json
{
  "customInstructions": "...(existing)...",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      { "matcher": "Bash", "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/approve-safe-commands.py", "timeout": 8 }] },
      { "matcher": "WebSearch", "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/suggest-docs-download.py", "timeout": 5 }] },
      { "matcher": "WebFetch", "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/suggest-docs-download.py", "timeout": 5 }] },
      {
        "matcher": "Task",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code pre-task" }]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Task",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code post-task" }]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "TodoWrite",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code post-todo" }]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code session-start" }] }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code session-end" }] }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit" }] }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "python3 ~/.claude/hooks/hpc-folder-structure-validator.py", "timeout": 30 }] },
      { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "cd /hpc/compgen/projects/llm_GEO_project/harmonia_metadata_agent/analysis/dstoker/harmonia && entire hooks claude-code stop" }] }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Downsides of Option 2:**
- Hardcoded absolute path to the harmonia repo in your **global** config — fires on every Claude Code session in every project, even ones that have nothing to do with Entire/harmonia
- The `entire` commands would error (silently, hopefully) when you're working in a different project without a `.entire/` directory
- Pollutes your global settings with project-specific concerns

**Option 1** is cleaner because the hooks only fire when you're working in this project. The same `cd` prefix is needed, but it's scoped to the right project. Want me to go ahead and implement Option 1?

